## Acceptance checklist (the judge verifies each item; build so every item is visibly true)
{{ acceptance }}

## DO
- Animate with time: every sampled frame (t = {{ judge_times }}) must differ visibly; continuous motion,
  no hard cuts, no per-frame random seeds.
- Aspect-correct coordinates: `p = (fragCoord - 0.5*u_resolution) / u_resolution.y` (circles stay round).
- Layer the passes from the table: background → midground → foreground → grade (vignette, tonemap, gamma).
- Use the style's palette literally (write the colour constants at the top); keep mean brightness in a
  readable range (neither near-black nor blown-out); tonemap `c/(1+c)` then gamma.
- Detail at several scales (fbm octaves, hash-placed elements, highlights) — the judge scores richness.
- Guard the maths: `x / max(d, 1e-4)`, `sqrt(max(x, 0.0))`, `normalize` only non-zero vectors,
  `clamp` acos/asin inputs — one NaN pixel caps the score at 0.
- Constant loop bounds; keep per-pixel cost sane (≤ ~100 raymarch steps, ≤ 8 fbm octaves).

## DON'T
- No `#version` line, no `uniform`/`out` declarations of the harness names (shader); no window,
  context creation, clock, file IO outside src/ (program).
- No placeholders ("TODO", "simplified"); no static image when the plan says motion.
- No textures other than the harness ones; no network; no imports outside the contract's allow-list.

